  'draft', 'core',
  'A 39-year-old woman with type 2 diabetes attends for review 3 months after starting a sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitor and having her HbA1c fall from 95 to 61 mmol/mol. Retinal screening at this visit shows new cotton wool spots and a small increase in the number of blot haemorrhages compared with her screening result 4 months earlier, though she remains classified as having moderate non-proliferative diabetic retinopathy at both time points.',
  'What is the most appropriate interpretation and management of these interval retinal changes?',
  array['diabetic retinopathy','early worsening with rapid glycaemic improvement','monitoring not treatment change']
