  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 56-year-old man with type 2 diabetes and diabetic macular oedema has been receiving 8-weekly intravitreal aflibercept for 2 years with a good anatomical response (resolved subretinal and intraretinal fluid), and visual acuity has stabilised at 6/9. He is now finding it increasingly difficult to attend appointments due to caring responsibilities and asks whether he can stop treatment.',
  'What is the most appropriate approach to discussing treatment discontinuation?',
  array['diabetic macular oedema','treatment discontinuation','extended treat-and-extend']
),
