  'draft', 'advanced',
  $x$A 27-year-old woman with known sarcoidosis (biopsy-confirmed, on no current systemic therapy) presents with bilateral panuveitis, vitreous 'snowball' opacities, and periphlebitis with candle-wax drippings on fundoscopy. Visual acuity is 6/12 bilaterally. Chest CT shows stable bilateral hilar lymphadenopathy. She has been started on topical corticosteroids with only partial improvement in anterior chamber activity, and vitreous inflammation persists at 6 weeks with new macular oedema on OCT.$x$,
  'What is the most appropriate next step in management?',
  array['sarcoid panuveitis','systemic corticosteroids','posterior segment inflammation']
),
