  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 60-year-old woman develops bilateral granulomatous panuveitis with serous retinal detachments 10 days after undergoing emergency vitrectomy and scleral repair for a penetrating injury to her left eye following a workplace accident. She now has photophobia, blurred vision, and mutton-fat keratic precipitates in her previously uninjured right eye as well as the injured left eye. Vitiligo-like skin changes are noted on examination.',
  'What is the most appropriate management approach?',
  array['sympathetic ophthalmia','bilateral granulomatous panuveitis','enucleation timing']
),
