  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 48-year-old woman with granulomatous panuveitis, bilateral serous retinal detachments, tinnitus, and new patchy alopecia and poliosis is diagnosed with Vogt-Koyanagi-Harada disease after lumbar puncture confirms a pleocytosis. She is started on high-dose oral prednisolone (1 mg/kg) with rapid initial improvement in vision, but her ophthalmologist plans a very prolonged, slow taper over at least 6 months rather than a rapid reduction once inflammation initially settles.',
  'What is the rationale for this prolonged corticosteroid tapering strategy?',
  array['Vogt-Koyanagi-Harada disease','corticosteroid tapering','chronic recurrent uveitis prevention']
),
