  'draft', 'advanced',
  $x$A 68-year-old man with hypertension and type 2 diabetes presents with acute-onset horizontal diplopia, worse in right gaze, associated with a droopy right eyelid. Examination reveals a right ptosis, the right eye deviated 'down and out', and the pupil is 4 mm and sluggishly reactive on the right compared to 2.5 mm and briskly reactive on the left. He reports no headache.$x$,
  'What is the most appropriate next step in management?',
  array['third nerve palsy','pupil involvement','posterior communicating artery aneurysm']
),
