  'draft', 'core',
  'A 74-year-old woman with atrial fibrillation (not anticoagulated due to previous gastrointestinal bleeding) presents with a transient episode of painless monocular visual loss in her right eye lasting approximately 8 minutes, described as a curtain descending, which has now fully resolved. Fundoscopy is unremarkable. She has no other neurological symptoms.',
  'What is the most appropriate immediate management?',
  array['amaurosis fugax','transient ischaemic attack','urgent stroke pathway']
),
('d8000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000041', 'mrcp2', '070e1d5d-829f-4fb7-ade1-9691bdff53dc',
  'draft', 'advanced',
